── unknown constraint
✗ unknown validation constraint

    playground_test.typo field "email" uses constraints go-playground does not know:
    emai

  This is almost always a typo — "emai" for "email", "uuid5" for
  "uuid4". The library panics on an unknown tag when it VALIDATES, so
  catching it here is the difference between a boot failure and a
  production crash on the first request that touches this field.

  Register your own with:

      playground.New(playground.Register("emai", func(v any) bool { ... }))

── not a struct
✗ cannot validate string

    A request type must be a struct: constraints live on fields, and a
    string has none.

  Wrap it — type Req struct { Value string `validate:"required"` } — or
  turn validation off for this application with validate.None().
